."],"released":"Apr 14, 2016","meta":79,"langs":["English","French"],"min":[["OS","Windows 7"],["Processor","intel core 2 DUO 2GHz +, AMD Athlon TMX2 2.2GHz +"],["Memory","2 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GT 705, AMD Radeon R7 240"],["Storage","7 GB available space"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows 8/10"],["Processor","intel core I5-4440, AMD FX 6300"],["Memory","4 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GT 740, AMD Radeon R7 250"],["Storage","7 GB available space"]],"deck":0,"blurb":"You play Abigail Blackwood, a young woman who has risen from the grave as a ghost, in this point-and-click adventure. Forty years have passed since her family's mad experiments, and she knows nothing of what followed. Exploring the ruined village of Oakmarsh near Coventry and the remains of Blackwood Manor, she pieces together how the household came to fall.\n\nThe game is a 2D Victorian mystery spread across more than 90 rooms in five distinct areas. Its mood is gothic and story-led, built around exploration and puzzle solving rather than action. It is a single-player experience that suits fans of classic point-and-click adventures who like a ghostly, atmospheric setting."}}